      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) Missing unmute handling across AAOS camera privacy state transitions: When transitioning between ENABLED and ENABLED_EXCEPT_ALLOWLISTED_APPS in onSensorPrivacyStateChanged(), SensorPrivacyService keeps isCombinedToggleSensorPrivacyEnabled(CAMERA) \u003d\u003d true, so AppOpsManager will not fire BasicClient::opChanged() to unmute allowlisted clients that were muted in ENABLED. Any handler for onSensorPrivacyStateChanged() that mutes clients via setCameraMute(true) must also restore setCameraMute(mOverrideCameraMuteMode) for active clients whose effective camera privacy is disabled in the new state (e.g., when transitioning to ENABLED_EXCEPT_ALLOWLISTED_APPS or DISABLED).\n\n2) Incomplete camera privacy check: Calling mSensorPrivacyPolicy-\u003eisCameraPrivacyEnabled(toString16(pkgName)) directly bypasses CameraService::isCameraPrivacyEnabled(...), which additionally accounts for automotive exterior system camera exemptions (isAutomotivePrivilegedClient \u0026\u0026 isAutomotiveExteriorSystemCamera) and android.permission.CAMERA_PRIVACY_ALLOWLIST (hasPermissionsForCameraPrivacyAllowlist). Consider encapsulating the shared per-client visibility/privacy/mute policy on BasicClient so opChanged() and onSensorPrivacyStateChanged() do not diverge.",
